==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[enrol]] {{qualifier|UK}} {{qualifier|CA}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|enroller|lang=fro}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-enroll.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[enter]] (a name, etc.) in a [[register]], [[roll]] or [[list]]
#* Prescott
#*: All the citizen capable of bearing arms '''enrolled''' themselves.
#* Milton
#*: An unwritten law of common right, so engraven in the hearts of our ancestors, and by them so constantly enjoyed and claimed, as that it needed not '''enrolling'''.
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[enlist]] (someone) or make (someone) a [[member]] of
#: ''They were eager to '''enroll''' new recruits.''
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To [[enlist]] oneself (in something) or become a [[member]] (of something)
#: ''Have you '''enrolled''' in classes yet for this term?''
# {{context|obsolete|transitive|lang=en}} To [[envelop]]; to [[enwrap]].
#: {{rfquotek|Spenser}}

====Synonyms====
